        "Consider a simple example: a cup of coffee that cost a small amount decades ago might now cost several times more, even though the coffee bean itself has not fundamentally changed. This gradual increase reflects inflation at work.",
        "To measure inflation accurately, economists rely on a tool called the Consumer Price Index, or CPI. This index tracks the average price of a large basket of common goods and services, such as food, housing, and transportation, comparing how these prices change from year to year.",
